WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.060
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.630
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:18.363
Unit seventeen: Writing: Coherence, Cohesion and Vocabulary. Today you will link ideas clearly and use precise, varied vocabulary.

4
00:00:18.663 --> 00:00:21.350
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.171
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:28.157
Coherence.

7
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.729
Coherence means clear and logical organisation of ideas.

8
00:00:33.317 --> 00:00:35.235
Good coherence helps the reader.

9
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.479
Your turn. Say: Coherence.

10
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:42.613
Coherence.

11
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.398
Cohesion.

12
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:48.277
Cohesion means the way sentences are linked together.

13
00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:50.906
Cohesion needs linking words.

14
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.157
Your turn. Say: Cohesion.

15
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:57.815
Cohesion.

16
00:00:58.550 --> 00:00:59.342
Linker.

17
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.814
Linker means a word that connects ideas.

18
00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:04.766
However is a linker.

19
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.898
Your turn. Say: Linker.

20
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:11.688
Linker.

21
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.544
Referencing.

22
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.221
Referencing means using words like this or they to refer back.

23
00:01:18.817 --> 00:01:21.118
Use referencing to avoid repetition.

24
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:24.485
Your turn. Say: Referencing.

25
00:01:27.333 --> 00:01:28.567
Referencing.

26
00:01:29.317 --> 00:01:30.422
Collocation.

27
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:34.078
Collocation means words that often go together.

28
00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:36.764
Make a decision is a collocation.

29
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:40.769
Your turn. Say: Collocation.

30
00:01:43.633 --> 00:01:44.960
Collocation.

31
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:46.811
Paraphrase.

32
00:01:47.817 --> 00:01:50.664
Paraphrase means to say something in different words.

33
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.878
Paraphrase the question.

34
00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:56.194
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

35
00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.220
Paraphrase.

36
00:02:00.983 --> 00:02:02.170
Repetition.

37
00:02:03.183 --> 00:02:05.984
Repetition means using the same word too often.

38
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:08.084
Avoid repetition.

39
00:02:08.683 --> 00:02:11.080
Your turn. Say: Repetition.

40
00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:14.981
Repetition.

41
00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:16.404
Formal.

42
00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:20.090
Formal means suitable for academic writing.

43
00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:22.149
Use formal language.

44
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.089
Your turn. Say: Formal.

45
00:02:27.933 --> 00:02:28.575
Formal.

46
00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:33.087
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.646
Visal, what are Coherence and Cohesion?

48
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:50.178
Coherence means your ideas follow a logical order. Cohesion means you link sentences with words like however, therefore and for example, and with referencing words like this and they.

49
00:02:51.283 --> 00:02:52.830
Should I use many linkers?

50
00:02:53.917 --> 00:03:02.075
No. Overusing linkers makes your writing sound mechanical. Use a few accurate linkers and let the ideas flow naturally.

51
00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.136
How can I improve vocabulary?

52
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:17.006
Learn collocations such as make progress and play a role, and paraphrase instead of repeating words. Use formal language, and avoid words you are not sure about.

53
00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.073
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:25.865
Grammar focus: Strategy: link ideas naturally, vary vocabulary.

55
00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:27.398
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:31.488
Pollution is rising; therefore, governments must act now.

57
00:03:32.383 --> 00:03:35.312
People should make a decision, not do a decision.

58
00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:44.724
Plan the order of ideas, link them with a few accurate linkers, and use referencing to avoid repetition. Learn collocations and paraphrase key words.

59
00:03:45.483 --> 00:03:49.947
Be careful! Don't say: I use however in every sentence.

60
00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.037
Say: I use a few accurate linkers.

61
00:03:55.337 --> 00:03:57.105
Do not overuse linkers.

62
00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.541
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:02.950
Improving a Paragraph.

64
00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:06.492
Mina writes a paragraph with the word important in every sentence.

65
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.299
Her teacher shows her how to paraphrase it as essential and significant.

66
00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.867
She adds the linkers however and therefore only where they are needed.

67
00:04:16.867 --> 00:04:20.236
She uses this and they to refer back and avoid repetition.

68
00:04:21.233 --> 00:04:23.837
Her next essay sounds clearer and more natural.

69
00:04:24.933 --> 00:04:28.761
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:29.617 --> 00:04:31.314
Coherence means blank.

71
00:04:31.614 --> 00:04:36.615
A, a long essay. B, big handwriting. C, logical organisation.

72
00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.979
The answer is C: logical organisation.

73
00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.350
Which is a linker?

74
00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:48.943
A, however. B, important. C, pollution.

75
00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.244
The answer is A: however.

76
00:04:55.383 --> 00:04:57.998
Overusing linkers makes writing sound blank.

77
00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:01.836
A, formal. B, mechanical. C, natural.

78
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.376
The answer is B: mechanical.

79
00:05:08.517 --> 00:05:10.330
Make a decision is a blank.

80
00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:14.690
A, verb tense. B, title. C, collocation.

81
00:05:18.233 --> 00:05:20.929
The answer is C: collocation.

82
00:05:22.083 --> 00:05:24.153
Mina replaced important with blank.

83
00:05:24.453 --> 00:05:27.978
A, essential. B, simple. C, tiny.

84
00:05:31.533 --> 00:05:33.544
The answer is A: essential.

85
00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:38.024
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:38.883 --> 00:05:42.276
How do you improve cohesion and vocabulary in your writing?

87
00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.607
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:52.907 --> 00:06:08.217
I plan the order of my ideas so the essay is coherent. I link sentences with a few accurate linkers and use referencing words to avoid repetition. I also learn collocations and paraphrase key words instead of repeating them.

89
00:06:08.517 --> 00:06:10.481
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:11.383 --> 00:06:17.971
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: link ideas naturally, vary vocabulary.

91
00:06:18.271 --> 00:06:22.642
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

92
00:06:22.942 --> 00:06:25.362
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:25.662 --> 00:06:28.674
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

